//@version=6
indicator("MNQ Reversal Blocks — 60-point session blocks, PRIME day-after zones, strict candle-close grading", shorttitle = "RevBlocks",
     overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500)

// ============================================================================
// WHAT THIS IS
//   Reversal blocks 60 points deep at session levels, drawn BEFORE price gets
//   there, only with the daily trend behind them, and graded strictly on this
//   chart's own candle closes. One kind of block, PRIME, is marked in advance:
//   it is the only one that goes on to a 100-point reversal far more often
//   than block size alone explains. Grade A PRIME blocks did it 80% of the
//   time in ten years of data.
//
//   A BLOCK starts at a level known in advance and extends 60 points beyond it:
//     AS  Asia session high / low, 18:00-03:00   (drawn at 03:00 ET)
//     18:00 open price                           (drawn at 03:00 ET)
//     midnight open price                        (drawn at 03:00 ET)
//     LO  London session high / low, 03:00-09:30 (drawn at 09:30 ET)
//     OR  opening range high / low, 09:30-10:00  (drawn at 10:00 ET)
//     09:30 open price                           (drawn at 10:00 ET)
//     IB  first-hour high / low, 09:30-10:30     (drawn at 10:30 ET)
//     PD / PW  prior day / prior week high and low: OFF by default. They are
//              the levels where a block held least often in ten years of data.
//   The open prices are support while price is above them and resistance
//   while below. A block is drawn only while price is still outside it, and
//   not on top of a live block on the same side. Nothing is ever moved or
//   painted backwards.
//
//   TREND   support blocks (longs) are drawn only when yesterday's close is
//           above its 50-day average, resistance blocks (shorts) only when it
//           is below. So in a downtrend the chart shows shorts only, and in an
//           uptrend longs only, until the close crosses the average.
//
//   PRIME BLOCKS - the mechanism
//     The day after a strong day WITH the trend, the cash session's opening
//     push goes back through yesterday's close and takes out the overnight
//     low (the overnight high, in a downtrend), and usually fails there:
//     buyers who missed yesterday's move (sellers, in a downtrend) are
//     waiting. A block is a PRIME candidate from the moment it is drawn when
//     all of this is already known:
//       1. yesterday closed at least 0.75 average daily ranges away from the
//          close before it, in the direction of the daily trend
//       2. the block is on the trend's side and its level was made overnight:
//          Asia or London high / low, the 18:00 open or the midnight open
//       3. that level is on the FAR side of yesterday's close - below it for
//          support, above it for resistance - by no more than 0.40 average
//          daily ranges
//     The first touch then decides the grade:
//       PRIME A   first touched 09:30-10:00 ET, the opening push
//       PRIME B   first touched 10:00-16:00 ET
//     Touched before 09:30 or after 16:00, it is an ordinary block.
//     "Yesterday's close" is the close of the last candle that starts before
//     16:15 ET, read from this chart, so it does not depend on how the daily
//     bar's close is set. About 45 candidates are drawn a year; about 8
//     become grade A and 7 grade B.
//
//   GRADING - STRICT (every candle of this chart, at its close)
//     TOUCH    a candle trades into the block
//     HIT      price reverses 45 points from the extreme it made at the block
//     BROKEN   a candle CLOSES beyond the far side of the block before the
//              hit. Wicks through the block are not a break; a candle that
//              closes beyond the block breaks it whatever its wick did.
//     100+     a block that was hit went on to reverse 100 points, still
//              without any candle closing beyond it
//     OPEN     touched, neither hit nor broken by the end of the next trade day
//   Hit rate = HIT / (HIT + BROKEN). A block is never marked HIT after a
//   candle of this chart has closed beyond it.
//
//   SKIP RULE (off by default)   a block touched while fading the overnight
//   gap, a fast move or a stretched RSI is greyed out and graded separately.
//
// WHAT THE BACKTEST SAYS (README.md, backtest/rb_blocks.py)
//   Real 1-minute Nasdaq-100 data, 60-point blocks, HIT = 45 points, trend
//   filter on. Ten years = 2017-03 to 2026-11, sizes scaled to the price.
//   Went on to 100+ (share of graded blocks), number of blocks in brackets:
//
//                                 all blocks   PRIME A      PRIME B
//     5-min chart, 10 years         53.5%      79.7% (79)   70.0% (70)
//       of which before Nov 2022    53.1%      78.0% (50)   69.7% (33)
//       of which since Nov 2022     54.0%      82.8% (29)   70.3% (37)
//     3-min chart, 10 years         52.1%      79.7%        64.3%
//     10-min chart, 10 years        56.0%      82.3%        72.9%
//     15-min chart, 10 years        56.8%      81.0%        74.3%
//     30-min chart, 10 years        58.2%      78.5%        78.6%
//     1-min chart, 10 years         48.5%      72.2%        55.7%
//     5-min, last 4 years, fixed
//       60 / 100 points             52.9%      80.0% (20)   69.7% (33)
//       same rule on coin-flip
//       copies of the data          51.3%      53.3%        54.9%
//     real MNQ futures, 50 days     48.7%      none         1 (it went to 100+)
//
//   45-point hit rate, 5-min chart, 10 years: all blocks 75.9%, PRIME A 96.2%,
//   PRIME B 87.1%.
//   PRIME A by year, 5-min chart, went on to 100+: 80% 85% 100% 86% 70% 69%
//   80% 86% 83% 80% (2017 to 2026, 3 to 13 blocks a year).
//
//   READ THIS BEFORE TRADING IT
//   - Ordinary blocks: the hit rate is set by block depth against reversal
//     size. Coin-flip copies of the data score the same. 53% go on to 100
//     points. Fading their edge for 45 points, exit on the break close, won
//     60% of the time and LOST 6.4 points a block over ten years.
//   - PRIME A is the exception and it is rare: about 8 blocks a year. 79
//     blocks put the 80% somewhere between about 71% and 89%.
//   - The 80% holds on 3- to 15-minute charts. On a 1-minute chart, where a
//     single 1-minute close beyond the block breaks it, grade A scores 72%.
//     On charts above 30 minutes no candle starts between 09:30 and 10:00, so
//     there is no grade A.
//   - Fading a grade A edge for 45 points, exit on the break close: 82.3%
//     wins, +21.4 points a block (5-min, 10 years, 79 trades, before costs;
//     a loss averages 88 points).
//   - The rule was found on this same ten-year history: first the day, then
//     the side of yesterday's close, then the time of the touch. Each step
//     held in both halves and on a wider set of levels, but none of it has
//     been traded forward.
//
//   The scorecard grades every block on this chart's own history.
// ============================================================================

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// INPUTS
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
const string G_BLK = "Blocks"
const string G_PRM = "PRIME blocks"
const string G_FLT = "Filters"
const string G_LVL = "Levels"
const string G_UI  = "Display"

blockPts = input.float(60.0, "Block depth, points", minval = 10.0, maxval = 60.0, step = 5.0, group = G_BLK)
hitPts   = input.float(45.0, "HIT = a reversal of at least this many points", minval = 5.0, step = 5.0, group = G_BLK,
     tooltip = "Backtested at 45 with 60-point blocks. A larger reversal lowers the hit rate: the scorecard shows the rate for several sizes.")
bigPts   = input.float(100.0, "Also mark when the reversal reaches this many points", minval = 10.0, step = 5.0, group = G_BLK)

usePrime  = input.bool(true, "Mark PRIME blocks", group = G_PRM,
     tooltip = "The day after a strong day with the daily trend, a block on the trend's side at an overnight level just beyond yesterday's close is PRIME. Grade A: first touched 09:30-10:00 New York time. Grade B: first touched 10:00-16:00. Backtest, 5-minute chart, 10 years: grade A 79.7% of 79 blocks went on to 100+, grade B 70.0% of 70, all other blocks 52.9%.")
primeMove = input.float(0.75, "Yesterday's close-to-close move with the trend, in average daily ranges: at least", minval = 0.5, maxval = 3.0,
     step = 0.05, group = G_PRM,
     tooltip = "Backtested at 0.75: 149 PRIME blocks in 10 years, 75.2% to 100+ (grades A and B together). At 0.5: 250 blocks, 66.8%. At 1.0: 74 blocks, 78.4%. At 1.25: 42 blocks, 85.7%. The samples above 0.75 are thin, and a wider test over all kinds of level did not confirm that a bigger move adds more.")
primeNear = input.float(0.40, "Level beyond yesterday's close by no more than this many average daily ranges", minval = 0.1, maxval = 1.0,
     step = 0.05, group = G_PRM,
     tooltip = "The level must sit on the far side of yesterday's close: below it for support, above it for resistance. Backtested at 0.40: 75.2% to 100+. At 0.30: 74.4%. At 0.50: 72.6%. At 0.60: 69.6%. Levels on the near side of the close: 58.5%.")
primeOnly = input.bool(false, "Show only PRIME blocks", group = G_PRM,
     tooltip = "Hides the ordinary blocks. They are still tracked and graded in the scorecard, so the numbers do not change.")

trendOnly = input.bool(true, "Draw a block only with the daily trend behind it", group = G_FLT,
     tooltip = "Support blocks when yesterday's close is above its 50-day average, resistance blocks when it is below. PRIME blocks are always on the trend's side.")
useSkips  = input.bool(false, "Skip blocks touched while fading the overnight gap, a fast move or a stretched RSI", group = G_FLT,
     tooltip = "Off by default: with the trend filter on, skipped blocks hit as often as the rest in the backtest. Skipped blocks are greyed out and graded separately in the scorecard.")

useAS = input.bool(true, "AS: Asia session high / low (18:00-03:00 ET)", group = G_LVL)
useGO = input.bool(true, "18:00 open price (drawn at 03:00 ET)", group = G_LVL)
useMO = input.bool(true, "Midnight open price (drawn at 03:00 ET)", group = G_LVL)
useLO = input.bool(true, "LO: London session high / low (03:00-09:30 ET)", group = G_LVL)
useOR = input.bool(true, "OR: opening range high / low (09:30-10:00 ET)", group = G_LVL)
useRO = input.bool(true, "09:30 open price (drawn at 10:00 ET)", group = G_LVL)
useIB = input.bool(true, "IB: first-hour high / low (09:30-10:30 ET)", group = G_LVL)
usePD = input.bool(false, "PD: prior day high / low (held least often in testing)", group = G_LVL)
usePW = input.bool(false, "PW: prior week high / low (held least often in testing)", group = G_LVL)

showDash   = input.bool(true, "Scorecard", group = G_UI)
showTags   = input.bool(true, "Label HIT / BROKEN / 100+ / SKIP", group = G_UI)
topColor   = input.color(#EF5350, "Resistance block", group = G_UI)
botColor   = input.color(#26A69A, "Support block", group = G_UI)
primeColor = input.color(#FFB300, "PRIME block outline", group = G_UI)
deadColor  = input.color(#787B86, "Broken / expired / skipped block", group = G_UI)

if not timeframe.isintraday
    runtime.error("Reversal Blocks grades intraday candles: use a 1 to 60 minute chart.")

float bigUse = math.max(bigPts, hitPts)

// The three skip conditions (fixed: these are the values that were tested).
const float GAP_ADR    = 0.3     // overnight gap, in average daily ranges
const float FAST_SIGMA = 2.0     // move over the last hour, in (average 5-minute range x sqrt(12))
const float RSI_HOT    = 75.0    // RSI(14) of 5-minute closes, into the block

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// COMPLETED HIGHER-TIMEFRAME BARS ONLY (never the bar in progress)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[pdH, pdL, pdC, sma50, adr] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D",
     [high[1], low[1], close[1], ta.sma(close, 50)[1], ta.sma(high - low, 14)[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[pwH, pwL] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W", [high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

// Daily trend: +1 yesterday closed above its 50-day average, -1 below, 0 unknown.
int bias = na(pdC) or na(sma50) or pdC == sma50 ? 0 : pdC > sma50 ? 1 : -1

// What was known before this candle opened, from completed 5-minute candles
// (the chart's own candles on charts above 5 minutes): the move over the last
// hour, the average candle range, and RSI(14).
bool   lowTF  = timeframe.in_seconds() <= 300
string featTF = lowTF ? "5" : timeframe.period
int    hourN  = lowTF ? 12 : math.max(1, math.round(3600.0 / timeframe.in_seconds()))

f_feat() =>
    float mv = close - close[hourN]
    float ar = ta.sma(high - low, 100)
    float rs = ta.rsi(close, 14)
    [mv[1], ar[1], rs[1]]

[fMove, fRange, fRsi] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, featTF, f_feat(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
float spd = fRange > 0 ? fMove / (fRange * math.sqrt(hourN)) : na

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// STATE
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
type Block
    int    side  = 0        // +1 resistance (top), -1 support (bottom)
    float  near  = na       // the level: where price enters the block
    float  far   = na       // a candle close beyond this breaks the block
    int    state = 0        // 0 waiting, 1 touched, 2 hit (still tracked for the larger reversal)
    float  turn  = na       // extreme made at the block so far
    float  best  = 0.0      // largest reversal from that extreme so far
    int    days  = 0        // trade-day changes since the touch
    bool   skip  = false    // skipped at the touch (graded separately)
    string name  = ""
    box    bx    = na
    bool   cand  = false    // PRIME candidate: decided when the block is drawn
    bool   prime = false    // its first touch came in the cash session: graded as PRIME
    bool   show  = true     // visible on the chart (false = hidden by "Show only PRIME blocks")
    bool   early = false    // PRIME, first touched 09:30-10:00: grade A (later touches are grade B)

type Tally
    int touched  = 0
    int hit      = 0
    int broken   = 0
    int expired  = 0
    int big      = 0
    int tTop     = 0
    int hTop     = 0
    int bTop     = 0
    int tBot     = 0
    int hBot     = 0
    int bBot     = 0
    int sTouched = 0        // skipped blocks, graded by the same rules
    int sHit     = 0
    int sBroken  = 0
    int drawn    = 0
    int pDrawn   = 0        // PRIME candidates drawn
    int pTouched = 0        // PRIME blocks: candidates first touched in the cash session
    int pHit     = 0
    int pBroken  = 0
    int pBig     = 0
    int aTouched = 0        // grade A: PRIME blocks first touched 09:30-10:00
    int aHit     = 0
    int aBroken  = 0
    int aBig     = 0

var array<Block> live  = array.new<Block>()
var array<float> bests = array.new<float>()     // best reversal of every graded block, capped at the larger size
var Tally tl = Tally.new()

var float asH = na
var float asL = na
var float loH = na
var float loL = na
var float orH = na
var float orL = na
var float ibH = na
var float ibL = na
var bool asDone = true
var bool loDone = true
var bool orDone = true
var bool ibDone = true
var float dayOpen = na      // the 18:00 ET open of this trade day
var float midOpen = na      // the first open after midnight ET
var float rthOpen = na      // the 09:30 ET open
var float gapADR  = na      // (09:30 open - yesterday's close) / average daily range, known from 09:30 on
var int dayCount = 0
var int pSeen    = 0        // PRIME candidates drawn before this candle

int  mod    = hour(time, "America/New_York") * 60 + minute(time, "America/New_York")
bool newDay = timeframe.change("D")
bool rth    = mod >= 570 and mod < 1020
bool cash   = mod >= 570 and mod < 960      // 09:30-16:00 ET: where a PRIME candidate must be touched first
bool opening = mod >= 570 and mod < 600     // 09:30-10:00 ET: a PRIME block first touched here is grade A

// "Yesterday's close" for the PRIME rule and the gap is read from this chart's
// own candles: the close of the last candle that starts before 16:15 ET. It
// does not depend on how the daily bar's close is set (last trade or
// settlement), and it is the price the backtest uses.
var float refClose = na     // that close for the trade day in progress
var float yC       = na     // for yesterday
var float yC2      = na     // for the day before yesterday
if newDay
    yC2 := yC
    yC  := refClose

// Yesterday's close-to-close move in average daily ranges, signed so that
// + = with the daily trend. A PRIME day needs at least `primeMove`.
float yMove    = bias == 0 or na(yC) or na(yC2) or na(adr) or adr <= 0 ? na : bias * (yC - yC2) / adr
bool  primeDay = usePrime and not na(yMove) and yMove >= primeMove

// Draw a block at `level` if the trend allows that side, price is still
// outside the block, and no live block on the same side overlaps it.
// `ovn`: the level was made overnight, before the cash session opens.
f_add(float level, int side, string name, bool ovn) =>
    float far = level + side * blockPts
    bool  ok  = not na(level) and side * (open - level) < 0 and not (trendOnly and (bias == 0 or side * bias > 0))
    if ok and live.size() > 0
        for b in live
            if b.side == side and math.min(b.near, b.far) <= math.max(level, far) and math.max(b.near, b.far) >= math.min(level, far)
                ok := false
    if ok
        float past = side * (level - yC)     // how far the level sits beyond yesterday's close (below it for support, above it for resistance)
        bool  pc   = primeDay and ovn and side * bias < 0 and past > 0 and past <= primeNear * adr
        bool  vis  = pc or not primeOnly
        color col  = side > 0 ? topColor : botColor
        color edg  = pc ? primeColor : col
        box   bx   = box.new(bar_index, math.max(level, far), bar_index + 1, math.min(level, far),
             border_color = color.new(edg, vis ? (pc ? 0 : 20) : 100), border_width = pc ? 2 : 1,
             bgcolor = color.new(col, vis ? (pc ? 78 : 85) : 100),
             text = vis ? (pc ? "PRIME · " + name + " · A if first touched 09:30-10:00, B until 16:00 ET" : name) : "",
             text_size = size.small, text_color = color.new(edg, vis ? 0 : 100), text_halign = text.align_right, text_valign = text.align_center)
        live.push(Block.new(side, level, far, 0, na, 0.0, 0, false, name, bx, pc, false, vis))
        tl.drawn += 1
        tl.pDrawn += pc ? 1 : 0

// A level that is support while price is above it and resistance while below.
f_addAuto(float level, string name, bool ovn) =>
    if not na(level) and open != level
        f_add(level, open < level ? 1 : -1, name, ovn)

// A PRIME candidate that can no longer be PRIME (first touched outside the
// cash session, or the cash session ended): from here on an ordinary block.
f_demote(Block b) =>
    color col = primeOnly ? deadColor : b.side > 0 ? topColor : botColor
    b.cand := false
    b.show := not primeOnly
    b.bx.set_border_width(1)
    b.bx.set_border_color(color.new(col, primeOnly ? 60 : 20))
    b.bx.set_bgcolor(color.new(col, primeOnly ? 93 : 85))
    b.bx.set_text_color(color.new(col, primeOnly ? 40 : 0))
    b.bx.set_text(primeOnly ? b.name + " · not PRIME: first touch outside 09:30-16:00 ET" : b.name)

// Why a block of this side would be skipped if it were touched on this candle
// ("" = it would not). Uses only what was known before the candle opened.
f_why(int s) =>
    float ex = s > 0 ? fRsi : 100.0 - fRsi
    not useSkips ? "" : not na(gapADR) and s * gapADR > GAP_ADR ? "gap fade" : not na(spd) and s * spd > FAST_SIGMA ? "fast move" :
         not na(ex) and ex >= RSI_HOT ? "RSI stretched" : ""

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1. NEW TRADE DAY: retire old blocks, draw the prior day / week blocks if enabled
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if newDay
    dayCount += 1
    if live.size() > 0
        for i = live.size() - 1 to 0
            Block b = live.get(i)
            bool waiting = b.state == 0
            if not waiting
                b.days += 1
            bool expire = not waiting and b.days >= 2
            if expire and b.state == 1 and not b.skip
                tl.expired += 1
            if expire and b.state == 2 and not b.skip
                bests.push(math.min(b.best, bigUse))
            if (waiting or expire) and b.state <= 1
                b.bx.set_right(bar_index)
            if (waiting or expire) and b.state <= 1 and b.show
                b.bx.set_border_width(1)
                b.bx.set_border_color(color.new(deadColor, 60))
                b.bx.set_bgcolor(color.new(deadColor, 93))
                b.bx.set_text_color(color.new(deadColor, 40))
            if waiting or expire
                live.remove(i)
    asH := na
    asL := na
    loH := na
    loL := na
    orH := na
    orL := na
    ibH := na
    ibL := na
    asDone := false
    loDone := false
    orDone := false
    ibDone := false
    dayOpen := open
    midOpen := na
    rthOpen := na
    gapADR  := na
    if usePD
        f_add(pdH, 1, "PD high", false)
        f_add(pdL, -1, "PD low", false)
    if usePW
        f_add(pwH, 1, "PW high", false)
        f_add(pwL, -1, "PW low", false)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 2. SESSION BLOCKS, each drawn on the first candle after its level is complete
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if mod < 180 and na(midOpen)
    midOpen := open
if mod >= 180 and mod < 1020 and not asDone
    asDone := true
    if useAS
        f_add(asH, 1, "AS high", true)
        f_add(asL, -1, "AS low", true)
    if useGO
        f_addAuto(dayOpen, "18:00 open", true)
    if useMO
        f_addAuto(midOpen, "midnight open", true)
if rth and not loDone
    loDone := true
    rthOpen := open
    gapADR  := na(yC) or na(adr) or adr <= 0 ? na : (open - yC) / adr
    if useLO
        f_add(loH, 1, "LO high", true)
        f_add(loL, -1, "LO low", true)
if rth and mod >= 600 and not orDone
    orDone := true
    if useOR
        f_add(orH, 1, "OR high", false)
        f_add(orL, -1, "OR low", false)
    if useRO
        f_addAuto(rthOpen, "09:30 open", false)
if rth and mod >= 630 and not ibDone
    ibDone := true
    if useIB
        f_add(ibH, 1, "IB high", false)
        f_add(ibL, -1, "IB low", false)

bool primeDrawnNow = tl.pDrawn > pSeen      // a PRIME candidate was drawn on this candle
pSeen := tl.pDrawn

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 3. GRADE every live block on this candle
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool touchNow      = false     // live: price is inside a block that was waiting
bool primeTouchNow = false     // live: price is inside a PRIME candidate, in the cash session
bool primeATouchNow = false    // live: ... in its opening half hour (grade A)
bool skipNow       = false     // live: price is inside a block that the skip rule rejects
bool hitNow        = false
bool bigNow        = false
bool brokeNow      = false

if live.size() > 0
    for i = live.size() - 1 to 0
        Block  b      = live.get(i)
        int    s      = b.side
        float  ext    = s > 0 ? high : low
        float  opp    = s > 0 ? low : high
        bool   inside = s * (ext - b.near) >= 0
        string why    = b.state == 0 and inside ? f_why(s) : ""
        if b.state == 0 and inside and why == "" and b.show
            touchNow := true
        if b.state == 0 and inside and why == "" and b.cand and cash
            primeTouchNow := true
        if b.state == 0 and inside and why == "" and b.cand and opening
            primeATouchNow := true
        if b.state == 0 and inside and why != "" and b.show
            skipNow := true
        if b.state <= 1
            b.bx.set_right(bar_index + 1)
        if barstate.isconfirmed
            bool first = false
            if b.cand and b.state == 0 and not inside and mod >= 960
                f_demote(b)                                 // the cash session ended with the candidate untouched
            if b.state == 0 and inside
                b.state := 1
                b.turn  := ext
                first   := true
                b.prime := b.cand and cash
                b.early := b.prime and opening
                if b.prime
                    b.bx.set_text((b.early ? "PRIME A · " : "PRIME B · ") + b.name)
                if b.cand and not b.prime
                    f_demote(b)                             // first touched outside the cash session: an ordinary block
                if why == ""
                    tl.touched += 1
                    tl.tTop += s > 0 ? 1 : 0
                    tl.tBot += s < 0 ? 1 : 0
                    tl.pTouched += b.prime ? 1 : 0
                    tl.aTouched += b.early ? 1 : 0
                if why != ""
                    b.skip := true
                    tl.sTouched += 1
                if why != "" and b.show
                    b.bx.set_border_width(1)
                    b.bx.set_border_color(color.new(deadColor, 40))
                    b.bx.set_bgcolor(color.new(deadColor, 92))
                    b.bx.set_text_color(color.new(deadColor, 20))
                    b.bx.set_text(b.name + " · skip: " + why)
                if why != "" and b.show and showTags
                    label.new(bar_index, s > 0 ? high : low, "SKIP · " + why,
                         yloc = s > 0 ? yloc.abovebar : yloc.belowbar,
                         style = s > 0 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up,
                         color = color.new(deadColor, 30), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
            if b.state >= 1
                bool   beyond = s * (close - b.far) > 0     // this candle closed beyond the block
                bool   gone   = false
                bool   graded = not b.skip
                color  col    = b.prime ? primeColor : s > 0 ? topColor : botColor
                color  txc    = b.prime ? color.black : color.white
                string tag    = b.early ? "PRIME A " : b.prime ? "PRIME B " : ""
                // strict: a close beyond the block ends it, whatever the wick did
                if beyond and b.state == 1 and graded
                    tl.broken += 1
                    tl.bTop += s > 0 ? 1 : 0
                    tl.bBot += s < 0 ? 1 : 0
                    tl.pBroken += b.prime ? 1 : 0
                    tl.aBroken += b.early ? 1 : 0
                if beyond and b.state == 1 and graded and b.show
                    brokeNow := true
                    b.bx.set_border_width(1)
                    b.bx.set_border_color(color.new(deadColor, 30))
                    b.bx.set_bgcolor(color.new(deadColor, 90))
                    b.bx.set_text_color(color.new(deadColor, 20))
                if beyond and b.state == 1 and graded and b.show and showTags
                    label.new(bar_index, s > 0 ? high : low, tag + "BROKEN",
                         yloc = s > 0 ? yloc.abovebar : yloc.belowbar,
                         style = s > 0 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up,
                         color = color.new(deadColor, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
                if beyond and b.state == 1 and not graded
                    tl.sBroken += 1
                if beyond
                    gone := true
                if not beyond
                    float newturn = s * (ext - b.turn) > 0 ? ext : b.turn
                    if not first                            // the extreme was made on an earlier candle
                        b.best := math.max(b.best, s * (b.turn - opp))
                    b.best := math.max(b.best, s * (newturn - close))   // this candle's own extreme, confirmed by its close
                    b.turn := newturn
                    bool nowHit = b.state == 1 and b.best >= hitPts
                    bool nowBig = b.best >= bigUse
                    if nowHit
                        b.state := 2
                    if nowHit and graded
                        tl.hit  += 1
                        tl.hTop += s > 0 ? 1 : 0
                        tl.hBot += s < 0 ? 1 : 0
                        tl.pHit += b.prime ? 1 : 0
                        tl.aHit += b.early ? 1 : 0
                    if nowHit and graded and b.show
                        hitNow := true
                        b.bx.set_border_color(color.new(col, 0))
                        b.bx.set_border_width(b.prime ? 3 : 2)
                    if nowHit and not graded
                        tl.sHit += 1
                    if nowBig
                        gone := true
                    if nowBig and graded
                        tl.big  += 1
                        tl.pBig += b.prime ? 1 : 0
                        tl.aBig += b.early ? 1 : 0
                    if nowBig and graded and b.show
                        bigNow := true
                    if showTags and graded and b.show and (nowHit or nowBig)
                        string txt = nowHit and nowBig ? "HIT " + str.tostring(bigUse, "#") + "+" :
                             nowHit ? "HIT " + str.tostring(hitPts, "#") : str.tostring(bigUse, "#") + "+"
                        label.new(bar_index, s > 0 ? high : low, tag + txt,
                             yloc = s > 0 ? yloc.abovebar : yloc.belowbar,
                             style = s > 0 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up,
                             color = color.new(col, nowHit ? 10 : 45), textcolor = txc, size = size.tiny)
                if gone and graded
                    bests.push(math.min(b.best, bigUse))
                if gone
                    live.remove(i)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 4. SESSION RANGES and the day's reference close, updated after the candle has been graded
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if mod < 975 or mod >= 1080
    refClose := close
if mod >= 1080 or mod < 180
    asH := na(asH) ? high : math.max(asH, high)
    asL := na(asL) ? low : math.min(asL, low)
if mod >= 180 and mod < 570
    loH := na(loH) ? high : math.max(loH, high)
    loL := na(loL) ? low : math.min(loL, low)
if mod >= 570 and mod < 600
    orH := na(orH) ? high : math.max(orH, high)
    orL := na(orL) ? low : math.min(orL, low)
if mod >= 570 and mod < 630
    ibH := na(ibH) ? high : math.max(ibH, high)
    ibL := na(ibL) ? low : math.min(ibL, low)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// SCORECARD — this chart's own history, graded by the rules above
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
f_cell(table t, int c, int r, string s, color tc, string al) =>
    table.cell(t, c, r, s, text_color = tc, text_halign = al, text_size = size.small)

f_rate(int a, int b) =>
    a + b > 0 ? str.tostring(100.0 * a / (a + b), "#.#") + "%" : "—"

f_row(table t, int r, string name, color nc, int touched, int hits, int broken) =>
    f_cell(t, 0, r, name, nc, text.align_left)
    f_cell(t, 1, r, str.tostring(touched), color.white, text.align_right)
    f_cell(t, 2, r, str.tostring(hits), color.white, text.align_right)
    f_cell(t, 3, r, str.tostring(broken), color.white, text.align_right)
    f_cell(t, 4, r, f_rate(hits, broken), color.white, text.align_right)

if showDash and barstate.islast
    var table dash = table.new(position.top_right, 5, 18, bgcolor = color.new(#101418, 12),
         border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 75), frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(color.gray, 55))
    table.clear(dash, 0, 0, 4, 17)
    color dim     = color.new(color.silver, 0)
    int   graded  = tl.hit + tl.broken
    int   aGraded = tl.aHit + tl.aBroken
    int   bTouched = tl.pTouched - tl.aTouched      // grade B = PRIME blocks that are not grade A
    int   bHit     = tl.pHit - tl.aHit
    int   bBroken  = tl.pBroken - tl.aBroken
    int   bBig     = tl.pBig - tl.aBig
    int   bGraded  = bHit + bBroken
    // hit rate for four reversal sizes, from the best reversal of every graded block
    float sizeB = 0.6 * bigUse
    float sizeC = 0.75 * bigUse
    int   nb = bests.size()
    int   nA = 0
    int   nB = 0
    int   nC = 0
    int   nD = 0
    if nb > 0
        for v in bests
            nA += v >= hitPts ? 1 : 0
            nB += v >= sizeB ? 1 : 0
            nC += v >= sizeC ? 1 : 0
            nD += v >= bigUse ? 1 : 0
    float seven = nb >= 10 ? bests.percentile_linear_interpolation(30) : na

    f_cell(dash, 0, 0, "REVERSAL BLOCKS — SCORECARD (this chart's history, strict candle-close grading)", color.white, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 0, 4, 0)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 1, str.tostring(blockPts, "#") + "-pt blocks · HIT = " + str.tostring(hitPts, "#") +
         "-pt reversal before any candle closes beyond", dim, text.align_left)
    f_cell(dash, 1, 1, "touched",  dim, text.align_right)
    f_cell(dash, 2, 1, "hit",      dim, text.align_right)
    f_cell(dash, 3, 1, "broken",   dim, text.align_right)
    f_cell(dash, 4, 1, "hit rate", dim, text.align_right)

    f_row(dash, 2, "All graded blocks",        color.white, tl.touched,  tl.hit,  tl.broken)
    f_row(dash, 3, "Resistance blocks (tops)", topColor,    tl.tTop,     tl.hTop, tl.bTop)
    f_row(dash, 4, "Support blocks (bottoms)", botColor,    tl.tBot,     tl.hBot, tl.bBot)
    f_row(dash, 5, usePrime ? "PRIME A · first touched 09:30-10:00 (also counted above)" : "PRIME marking is off", primeColor,
         tl.aTouched, tl.aHit, tl.aBroken)
    f_row(dash, 6, usePrime ? "PRIME B · first touched 10:00-16:00 (also counted above)" : "PRIME marking is off", primeColor,
         bTouched, bHit, bBroken)
    f_row(dash, 7, useSkips ? "Skipped at the touch (graded separately)" : "Skip rule is off", dim, tl.sTouched, tl.sHit, tl.sBroken)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 8, "Went on to " + str.tostring(bigUse, "#") + "+ pts before any close beyond: all blocks " + str.tostring(tl.big) +
         " of " + str.tostring(graded) + " (" + f_rate(tl.big, graded - tl.big) + ") · PRIME A " + str.tostring(tl.aBig) +
         " of " + str.tostring(aGraded) + " (" + f_rate(tl.aBig, aGraded - tl.aBig) + ") · PRIME B " + str.tostring(bBig) +
         " of " + str.tostring(bGraded) + " (" + f_rate(bBig, bGraded - bBig) + ")", color.white, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 8, 4, 8)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 9, "Reversal of at least " + str.tostring(hitPts, "#") + " / " + str.tostring(sizeB, "#") + " / " +
         str.tostring(sizeC, "#") + " / " + str.tostring(bigUse, "#") + " pts:  " + f_rate(nA, nb - nA) + " / " +
         f_rate(nB, nb - nB) + " / " + f_rate(nC, nb - nC) + " / " + f_rate(nD, nb - nD), color.white, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 9, 4, 9)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 10, "7 in 10 blocks reversed at least " + (na(seven) ? "—" : str.tostring(seven, "#")) +
         " pts before any close beyond", color.white, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 10, 4, 10)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 11, "Drawn " + str.tostring(tl.drawn) + " blocks in " + str.tostring(dayCount) + " days (" +
         (dayCount > 0 ? str.tostring(1.0 * tl.drawn / dayCount, "#.#") : "—") + " a day), " + str.tostring(tl.pDrawn) +
         " of them PRIME candidates · " + str.tostring(live.size()) + " live now · " + str.tostring(tl.expired) +
         " touched but still open after two days", dim, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 11, 4, 11)

    string trendTxt = bias == 0 ? "DAILY TREND unknown (not enough daily history)" :
         "DAILY TREND " + (bias > 0 ? "UP" : "DOWN") + ": yesterday's close " + str.tostring(pdC, format.mintick) +
         (bias > 0 ? " is above" : " is below") + " its 50-day average " + str.tostring(sma50, format.mintick)
    string sideTxt = not trendOnly ? " · trend filter off: both sides drawn" :
         bias > 0 ? " · only support blocks (longs) are drawn until the close is back below the average" :
         bias < 0 ? " · only resistance blocks (shorts) are drawn until the close is back above the average" : " · no blocks drawn"
    f_cell(dash, 0, 12, trendTxt + sideTxt, bias > 0 ? botColor : bias < 0 ? topColor : dim, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 12, 4, 12)

    string moveTxt = na(yMove) ? "" : str.tostring(math.abs(yMove), "#.##") + " average daily ranges " +
         (yMove >= 0 ? "with" : "against") + " the trend"
    string needTxt = "PRIME needs " + str.tostring(primeMove, "#.##") + " with the trend"
    float  bandFar = na(yC) or na(adr) ? na : yC - bias * primeNear * adr
    string bandTxt = na(bandFar) ? "" : str.tostring(math.min(yC, bandFar), format.mintick) + " and " +
         str.tostring(math.max(yC, bandFar), format.mintick)
    string primeTxt = not usePrime ? "PRIME marking is off" : na(yMove) ? "PRIME: needs two completed days on the chart and the daily averages" :
         primeDay ? "PRIME DAY: yesterday closed " + moveTxt + ". " + (bias > 0 ? "Support" : "Resistance") +
         " blocks at overnight levels between " + bandTxt + (bias > 0 ? " (below" : " (above") +
         " yesterday's close) are PRIME: grade A if first touched 09:30-10:00 ET, grade B until 16:00" :
         "Not a PRIME day: yesterday closed " + moveTxt + " (" + needTxt + ")"
    f_cell(dash, 0, 13, primeTxt, primeDay ? primeColor : dim, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 13, 4, 13)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 14, "Backtest, 5-min chart, 10 years. All blocks: 75.9% hit, 53.5% went on to 100+ (5,283 blocks). Coin-flip data scores the same.",
         dim, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 14, 4, 14)
    f_cell(dash, 0, 15, "PRIME A: 96.2% hit, 79.7% went on to 100+ (79 blocks, about 8 a year; 78.0% before Nov 2022, 82.8% since). 15-min chart 81.0%, 1-min chart 72.2%.",
         primeColor, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 15, 4, 15)
    f_cell(dash, 0, 16, "PRIME B: 87.1% hit, 70.0% went on to 100+ (70 blocks). Coin-flip data: A 53%, B 55%. Fading a grade A edge for 45 pts, exit on the break close: 82.3% wins, +21.4 pts a block before costs.",
         dim, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 16, 4, 16)
    f_cell(dash, 0, 17, "Only PRIME blocks beat chance, on small samples (79 and 70 blocks in ten years). Every other block's hit rate comes from block depth, not prediction.",
         color.orange, text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 17, 4, 17)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ALERTS
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
alertcondition(primeDrawnNow, "PRIME block drawn", "Reversal Blocks: a PRIME block has been drawn. It counts as PRIME if price first touches it between 09:30 and 16:00 New York time")
alertcondition(primeATouchNow, "Price entered a PRIME block, grade A", "Reversal Blocks: price is inside a PRIME block in the opening half hour (09:30-10:00 ET): grade A")
alertcondition(primeTouchNow, "Price entered a PRIME block", "Reversal Blocks: price is inside a PRIME block (cash session, the day after a strong day with the trend)")
alertcondition(touchNow, "Price entered a reversal block", "Reversal Blocks: price is inside a block")
alertcondition(skipNow, "Price entered a block the skip rule rejects", "Reversal Blocks: price is inside a block, but it is fading the gap, a fast move or a stretched RSI")
alertcondition(hitNow, "Block hit", "Reversal Blocks: HIT — the reversal reached the hit size with no candle closing beyond the block")
alertcondition(bigNow, "Block reached the larger reversal", "Reversal Blocks: a block that was hit has reached the larger reversal")
alertcondition(brokeNow, "Block broken", "Reversal Blocks: a candle closed beyond a block before it was hit")
